  "selection_policy": "V30 beat Homa significantly on overall mean, P95, P99, queue mean, and queue P99, but its long-flow mean confidence interval crossed zero and its queue/Jain control gates failed. A frozen diagnostic sweep found that 16 ACK packets above the path BDP is the first same-leaf setting that preserved V30's seven-way 65536-byte incast result, while cross-leaf flows remain capped by the 8320-ns topology diameter. V31 exposed an ACTIVE-empty terminal transaction bug before performance could be read. The independently tested repair closes a zero-pending-ACK PREPARE or ACTIVATE generation before terminal reset and leaves every grant target unchanged. V32 reuses the frozen min(topology-diameter BDP, path BDP plus 16 MTU packets) rule, only raises the first gate for a whole flow that fits, and keeps that window after the first grant. Fresh seeds 230--234 and every gate are frozen before performance is read.",
